   $q$Which choice best describes the point of view of this story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A third-person narrator shares Arjun's thoughts and feelings.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Arjun tells the story himself, using the words \"I\" and \"me.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-first-and-third-person"},{"text":"A third-person narrator shares only Nani's private thoughts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-character-focus"},{"text":"Nani tells the story, describing how her grandson reacted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-narrator-with-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A third-person narrator shares Arjun's thoughts and feelings.$q$, $q$The narrator calls Arjun "he" but tells us what he thinks, such as that he "did not understand" the fuss about the moon. We only learn what Nani says aloud, never her private thoughts.$q$, 'draft', 'c9bf87f0-bfa9-5420-a8ad-7258ddba8f0c')
